.TH HOWDY.TOML 5 "@HOWDY_MAN_DATE@" "Howdy Next @PROJECT_VERSION@" "File Formats"
.SH NAME
howdy.toml \- Howdy Next configuration file
.SH DESCRIPTION
The file
.I @HOWDY_CONFIG_PATH_ROFF@
contains runtime configuration for Howdy Next.
.PP
The configuration file uses TOML syntax. Options are grouped into tables, and each
option is a key and a typed value:
.PP
.nf
[core]
disabled = false

[video]
device_path = "/dev/v4l/by-id/usb-camera-video-index0"
max_height = 320.0
timeout = 4
.fi
.PP
Booleans are written as
.B true
or
.BR false .
Integers are written without quotes.
Floating-point options accept integers or decimals.
Strings are enclosed in double quotes and must be printable ASCII; an empty string selects
the default value. Table and key names must be printable ASCII as well.
Lines beginning with
.B #
are comments.
Omitted options use the defaults listed below.
.PP
Howdy rejects unknown tables, unknown keys, and values of the wrong type, and then
fails closed.
.SH "CONFIGURATION OPTIONS"
@HOWDY_CONFIG_REFERENCE@
.SH FILES
.TP
.I @HOWDY_CONFIG_PATH_ROFF@
Main Howdy configuration file.
.SH "SEE ALSO"
.BR howdy (1),
.BR pam_howdy (8)
